senses.gloss:
अध्य्-√ आस् to sit down or lie down upon, to settle upon;
to occupy as one's seat or habitation;
to get into, enter upon;
to be directed to or upon;
to affect, concern;
to preside over, influence, rule;
to cohabit with:
Caus. P. अध्य्-आसयति, to cause to sit down, Bhaṭṭ. :
Desid. (p. अध्यासिसिषमाण) to be about to rise up to (acc.), Bhaṭṭ.

आ-√ ध्यै (cf. आ-√ धी) P. (p. -ध्यायत् [BhP. ix, 14, 43]; Impv. 2. sg. -ध्याहि [MBh.])
to meditate on;
to wish or pray for anything for another.
